21
00:01:04,801 --> 00:01:07,630
God's answer: send him to
the vineyard, and I will

22
00:01:07,630 --> 00:01:09,836
hide him in the shadow of the mountain.

23
00:01:10,286 --> 00:01:13,244
So in the morning, Jeremiah
hands him a basket.

24
00:01:13,244 --> 00:01:15,385
Bring figs, he says, for the sick.

25
00:01:15,835 --> 00:01:18,946
The heat is fierce.
Abimelech sits down under a

26
00:01:18,946 --> 00:01:21,595
tree, the basket beside him, and sleeps.

27
00:01:22,045 --> 00:01:25,842
That same morning, the army closes
in. What will he wake up to?

28
00:01:27,792 --> 00:01:31,564
Did you know? Scholars think a
Jewish author wrote this story,

29
00:01:31,564 --> 00:01:34,789
probably in Hebrew, about
nineteen hundred years ago.

30
00:01:35,239 --> 00:01:38,053
No Hebrew copy survives. It lived on in

31
